  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nCold front enters the western zones of the CWA after 21Z today with \nanafrontal precipitation after 00Z Monday. Northwesterly winds bring \nin a sharply colder airmass into the area, marking a pattern change \nthat will take hold through the duration of the 7 day forecast. \nTight 850mb gradient in the wake of the front will translate to \nrapidly dropping temperatures tonight. Low 40s by morning, only \nrecovering into the mid to upper 40s Monday for high temperatures. \nBrief lake effect precipitation possible Monday night. This could be \nin the form of light snow inland in NW PA with only a light coating \nexpected. Area wide temperatures Monday night expected to be in the \n20s away from the lakeshore, and 303-5F adjacent to it. Dry and \nclearer Tuesday night with the lowest temperatures in the 7 day \nforecast, down to near 20F in the outlying areas of NE OH and NW PA. \nNext chances for significant precipitation come Thursday/Friday from \na possible coastal low pressure system.",
